    "label": "35",
    "prompt": "Rationalise the denominator and simplify. $\\dfrac2{3-\\sqrt3}$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1+\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{3}$.\n\nMultiply numerator and denominator by the conjugate $3+\\sqrt3$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac2{3-\\sqrt3}&=\\frac2{3-\\sqrt3}\\times\\frac{3+\\sqrt3}{3+\\sqrt3}\\\\\\frac2{3-\\sqrt3}&=\\frac{2(3+\\sqrt3)}{9-3}\\\\\\frac2{3-\\sqrt3}&=\\frac{3+\\sqrt3}{3}\\\\\\frac2{3-\\sqrt3}&=1+\\frac{\\sqrt3}{3}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 24
  },
